// Pebble Prix: a three-lap race round a coastal village, four little roadsters (you and three computer
// drivers). The car drives itself forward; it steers toward the pointer (where the pointer is relative
// to the car on screen). Hold the press through a sharp turn to drift: the rear slides out, the tyres
// smoke, and a drift held long enough fires a boost when you let go (or straighten out). Grass and sand
// slow you, walls and barrels bounce you, boost strips push you. 1ST to 4TH, lap times, a best lap.
//
// Touch: the pointer only moves while a finger is down, so a finger steers by dragging, and lifting it
// holds the car's heading; a drag held sharply to one side is the drift, lifting the finger (or
// straightening the drag) lets it go. With a mouse, hovering steers and a press drifts the same way.
//
